      "sha256": "6f19f8363f75963c69072f03aa7515ffa304d6b726f85b09188760ae682e3447",
      "bytes": 1456,
      "line_count": 13,
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line": 1,
          "text": "The expr language has no error handling: runtime errors cause unrecoverable panics."
        },
        {
          "line": 3,
          "text": "Add comprehensive error handling:"
        },
        {
          "line": 4,
          "text": "- `try(expression, fallback)` - returns expression result on success or the lazily-evaluated fallback on error; requires exactly two arguments."
        },
        {
          "line": 5,
          "text": "- `try { expr } catch { handler }` - block form; optionally `catch <name> { ... }` to bind the error."
        },
        {
          "line": 6,
          "text": "- `catch <name> is \"substring\" { ... }` - catches only errors whose message contains the substring;"
        },
        {
          "line": 7,
          "text": "- `finally { cleanup }` - optional clause that always executes after try/catch; if the finally body throws, that error propagates (overriding any prior result)."
        },
        {
          "line": 8,
          "text": "- `throw(value)` - throws a custom error from any value (the error message is its string conversion); requires exactly one argument."
        },
        {
          "line": 9,
          "text": "- `retry` - usable inside catch blocks, re-executes the try body; automatic limit of three retries before raising a distinct exhaustion error. Using retry outside a catch block raises a runtime error."
        },
        {
          "line": 10,
          "text": "- `errtype(err)` - classifies a caught error; requires exactly one argument. Returns:"
        },
        {
          "line": 11,
          "text": "  - `\"index\"` for out-of-range/bounds errors, `\"conversion\"` for type-conversion failures, `\"type\"` for type-mismatch/assertion errors, `\"nil\"` for nil-pointer/reference errors, `\"retry\"` for retry-exhaustion errors, `\"custom\"` for all other errors including those from `throw`, `\"none\"` when the inp"
        },
        {
          "line": 13,
          "text": "IMPORTANT: Please work on this in a new branch from main and commit everything when you are done."
        }
      ]
    },
